=== 4. THE ONE REAL CONTRACT GAP, AND IT CLOSES INSIDE MY OWN FILE ===
`who` and `lead` are UIDs: party_invite calls get_hero(who) and parties.has(lead) is keyed by
LEADER UID. But a viewer types a NAME - "!party invite Bob". roster.gd has NO name->uid resolver
(get_hero is a bare uid-keyed dict lookup: `return heroes.get(user_id, {})`).
THIS NEEDS NO ENGINE ADDITION. Two facts close it:
  (a) `_hero_named(nm)` already exists in MY file at chatcmd.gd:657 - the !dice precedent
      (`!dice [stake] [name]`), iterating roster.heroes and comparing name.to_lower() == nm.
  (b) roster.fresh() writes `"id": user_id` INTO the hero dict, so the uid is recoverable from
      _hero_named()'s return value as String(h.get("id","")). No new resolver function is needed.
And _dice_line is the pattern for the unresolved case: answer "No hero named %s." % safe_word(arg2)
BEFORE calling the engine, rather than passing a name into a uid parameter and getting the engine's
"No hero by that name." for the wrong reason.
=> 42b's command surface is writable ENTIRELY inside scripts/chatcmd.gd + data/commands.json
   the moment the dict reaches main. ONE WINDOW, no engine dependency beyond the merge.

